[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186345274 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup \\{-{C}_{2}\\}\\cup \\{-{C}_{3}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ and $-{C}_{3}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fc8d5ef6-ad4d-51c7-8822-84767360e2eb" :activity/id #uuid "fc8d5ef6-ad4d-51c7-8822-84767360e2eb" :activity/title "Properties of Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049346 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-bd8e2704-5f40-5faf-b9f0-5291baf681f3" "step-271a47d9-c574-51a4-b4e3-461cef8bc255" "step-def0e380-3b81-5346-998d-cfdab0e48044" "step-b0747b36-5013-549d-a28a-aa3dd9ab1385" "step-5b83a2d9-8217-5e31-a5fa-035a5c1103a2"] :activity/first-step "step-bd8e2704-5f40-5faf-b9f0-5291baf681f3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-bd8e2704-5f40-5faf-b9f0-5291baf681f3" :step/id #uuid "bd8e2704-5f40-5faf-b9f0-5291baf681f3" :step/content 17592186326775 :step/next "step-271a47d9-c574-51a4-b4e3-461cef8bc255" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-271a47d9-c574-51a4-b4e3-461cef8bc255" :step/id #uuid "271a47d9-c574-51a4-b4e3-461cef8bc255" :step/content 17592186345274 :step/next "step-def0e380-3b81-5346-998d-cfdab0e48044" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-def0e380-3b81-5346-998d-cfdab0e48044" :step/id #uuid "def0e380-3b81-5346-998d-cfdab0e48044" :step/content 17592186424620 :step/next "step-b0747b36-5013-549d-a28a-aa3dd9ab1385" :db/ensur